    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0731" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1–NE/9–850:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gross</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-08T18:05:00-04:00">September 8,
                            1950—6:05 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 8—7:46 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>488. Jebb (UK) feels we should be prepared for action if Chinese Communists take
                    military action in Korea. He made suggestion in which we concur that this topic
                    should be on agenda for FM meetings.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d503-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gross</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d503-f1" n="11" xml:id="d503-f1-content">
                <p>The Department of State’s reply, in telegram 243, September 12, read as follows:
                    “Korea on agenda FM mtgs reurtel 488, Sept 8, and
                    aspect question to which Jebb refers can readily be raised as part of genl
                    Korean discussion.” (390.1–NE/9–850)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
